    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b9b9e5a_6aa5629a",
        "filename": "src/utils/SkShadowUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 678,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-28T18:09:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you know that information there, then that would be the place to do it and we can avoid all this. We do have a bit of a transform boogaloo where we apply the inverse CTM to the lightPos before storing it in the ShadowRec, and then reapply the current CTM when we draw using the ShadowRec. This is used for cases where\nwe\u0027re tiling which I don\u0027t think we\u0027re doing here. In that case, the CTMs will be the same and it should have no effect.\n\nThe directional light flag doesn\u0027t come into play because at this point Android doesn\u0027t use directional lights. If -- after some discussion with UX -- we decide to make that switch, then we can remove the preTransform as it won\u0027t be needed then.",
      "parentUuid": "21ad4b36_1d672fed",
      "revId": "56b7a0509260700805344616caca54664cd9052a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
